From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: glacier <hyouga.dev@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 1 Sep 2026 02:05:19 +0900
Subject: [PATCH] Let a dry section answer the liquid box scans without reading
 a block

Every entity runs handleWaterMovement once a tick, and it walks its own bounding box a
block at a time asking each one whether it is water. In a profile at 0218 that scan was
13.31% of the server thread, 7.79% of it in the loop itself, with isMaterialInBB - the
same walk for lava, from isInLava - another 3.39%. Almost no entity is ever in either
liquid, so the scan that finds nothing is the common case rather than the rare one.

ChunkSection already counts the blocks it holds that are not air and the ones that tick.
Counting the water and the lava too costs one comparison per block written, and it lets
handleMaterialAcceleration, isMaterialInBB and isAABBInMaterial ask whether any section
their box touches holds that liquid at all - a handful of int loads - before walking
anything. This is the shape patch 0218 used for the collision query: skip the query, not
just the work inside it.

Anything the counters cannot answer is answered true and scanned exactly as before: a
chunk that is not loaded (the scan itself may load it, and that must not change), world
decoration in flight, or any material other than water and lava. Water and lava are
counted separately so that a section on the sea floor does not send every isInLava call
back to the full walk.

A count that drifts below the truth would silently stop an entity from noticing it is
standing in water, so it is verified from both ends. ChunkSectionLiquidCountTest walks a
section through 20,000 random writes - liquid over liquid, liquid over air, air over
liquid, solid over liquid - and recounts all 4096 blocks after each of the first thousand
and periodically after that, and covers recalcBlockCounts and the bulk load constructor
as well. AthenaIndexAudit gained a section recount, one chunk per tick round robin, which
covers the load path the unit test cannot: 52,074 section checks over a run, 26,687 of
them holding liquid, no mismatches.

Measured +4.79% TPS, 6/6 pairwise wins, at 30,000 golems with four bots. Two of the six
pairs were disturbed by unrelated disk load on the machine; their ratios were 1.0115 and
1.0576, and the four clean pairs span 1.0408 to 1.0614.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>

